   <text:p text:style-name="P102" loext:marker-style-name="T37"><text:span text:style-name="T37">The next screen shows a list of the devices that have been observed by DeployGate or that were included in the provisioning profile. Your new device entry will show up on the screen with a </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T45">Not Exist</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T37"> entry. Make sure that the entry for the new device is checked and then press the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T45">Export Selected UDIDs</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T37"> button. This will create a file “multiple-device-upload-ios.txt” that can be used on the Apple Developer website to add these devices to the mobile provisioning file.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P44" loext:marker-style-name="T37"/>
