   <text:p text:style-name="P44" loext:marker-style-name="T37"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P65" loext:marker-style-name="T37"><text:span text:style-name="T37">At this point your device has been registered to your Apple Developer account. <text:s/>You now need to add the device to the provisioning profile for your app. <text:s/>Select the provisioning profile being used to test the app. Make sure your test device is checked in the list of devices at the bottom of the screen. Press </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T45">Generate</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T37">. <text:s/></text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P88" loext:marker-style-name="T37"><text:span text:style-name="T45">Note:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T37"> For the purposes of testing with DeployGate, an AdHoc type of provision profile must be created and used. If you have not selected AdHoc, the list of devices will not be available on the screen.</text:span></text:p>
